      "Nostalgia is a powerful drug, but wonderment in cinema often serves as a temporary escape rather than a structural shift in reality.\n\nChristos Tsiolkas on Cinema and Wonder\nEvidence: childhood awe, cinematic pleasure, aesthetic hope\n#Aletheia",
      "The claim is that cinema provides a vital return to wonder and magic, acting as a necessary balm for the adult soul.\nStated Judgement: (+0.5, 0.0) — Good Preference",
