      "Christos Tsiolkas reflects on the enduring power of wonderment in cinema, drawing parallels between classic films like E.T. and the human capacity to find magic in the fantastical.",
      "The Poison:\nExcessive reliance on nostalgia can sometimes act as a barrier to engaging with the complexities of the present moment.",
      "The Breakdown & Plane Error:\nThere is no plane error. The interrogative planes are satisfied; the WHY (meaning) is clearly articulated, and the EFFECT (resonance) matches the stated intent.",
