      "Mortgage rates remain elevated above 6%, creating a barrier for new buyers. This is presented as a market inevitability rather than a consequence of specific monetary policy decisions.",
      "The Poison:\nFraming this as a 'break' that buyers aren't getting masks the fact that the system is functioning exactly as intended for those who already own assets.",
      "The Breakdown & Plane Error:\nThe error is in the HOW (monetary policy) being treated as a natural phenomenon (WHAT). It ignores the WHO (the beneficiaries of high interest income vs. the victims of high borrowing costs).",
