      "Alethekanon:\nThe claim of 'no going back' is a rhetorical device to externalize responsibility. Strategic decisions, especially those with multi-decade implications, demand continuous re-evaluation. Failure to act on revision opportunities is a choice to accept the existing, potentially suboptimal, trajectory.",
